{
  "title": "Anticoagulation Medications",
  "url": "https://www.orthobullets.com/basic-science/9054/anticoagulation-medications",
  "subtitle": "Updated: Jun 3 2026",
  "sections": [
    {
      "text": "Introduction",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "The coagulation cascade comprises a series of reactions that lead to **formation of fibrin**, which leads to **platelet activiation** and **clot formation**",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "4",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "an imbalance of the coagulation cascade can cause **thromboembolism** and **DVT**",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Virchow's triad describes risk factors for thromboembolism and DVT and includes",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "**venous stasis**",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "**endothelial damage**",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "**hypercoagulable state**",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Orthopaedic surgery predisposes high risk of thromboembolism and certain procedures may require anticoagulation",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "there are many choices of anticoagulants, each has advantages and disadvantages",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "chemical DVT prophylaxis may not be indicated in foot and ankle surgeries or isolated lower extremity fractures below the knee",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
